 $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta )$, where\n\n$$\nr=1,\\,\\theta ={120}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1\\operatorname{cos}⁡({120}^{∘}) \\\\  & =1(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1\\operatorname{sin}⁡({120}^{∘}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}).$" 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564602 1080 "(\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})" 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564602 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564602 1083 #uuid "224f63a5-963c-5451-b6e8-7fba150db1a5" 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564603 1080 "\\sqrt{3}" 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564603 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564603 1083 #uuid "22d5b185-f087-5184-aeb5-54dd0dedbfd5" 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564604 1080 "(\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{15}{2})" 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564604 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564604 1083 #uuid "2442c3e4-6efc-5e15-89f6-7d2d57190032" 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564605 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564605 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564605 1083 #uuid "248e1098-29d9-543b-83d4-0b32e84165eb" 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564606 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564616 13194139536073 17592186045443 true] [17592186564606 1068